  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Number of ambidentate ligands in a representative metal complex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>SCN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;[<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>en</mi><mo>=</mo></math>ethylenediamine]</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Ambidentate ligand has two or more donor atoms, but during complex formation, only one donor atom is attached to central metal.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>SCN</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ion has donor atoms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>.&nbsp;</p><p>Examples of ambidentate ligands include&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>. So,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>SCN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ligands are ambidentate.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/91e529c1-d7d5-4074-a83e-ad98848f21f8.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 86px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
